# ADR-deviation marker — cli#247 adjacent-shadow detection

- date: 2026-09-26
- branch: fix/247-shadow-detection
- adr_governing: ADR-002 (bassclef init safety contract); ADR-006 (install harness)
- outcome: ADR-honored

## Rationale

The change extends existing scripts. It adds one shared defensive function and three call sites plus a runbook amendment. It does not touch `bassclef init` itself. It does not touch the safety contract's path scoping, atomic writes, or escape-hatch matrix per ADR-002.

The check fires BEFORE init, in the smoke harness only. Adopters running `bassclef init` directly are not affected. The check is scoped to smoke-reset + smoke-one-shot + docker entry.sh — three harness surfaces owned by the CLI repo, not by adopter machines.

ADR-006 install harness names the runbook as the operator surface; the amendment extends the runbook without contradicting its five decision points.

No new ADR filed. Change stays within existing ADR envelope.
